WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.611
Week thirteen.

00:00:01.661 --> 00:00:03.888
What the final exam looks like.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.754
Five short scenario questions, worth six marks each.

00:00:07.804 --> 00:00:10.868
Thirty marks in total, all on the guest lectures.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:15.178
It's Monday the twenty third of November at one pm Check your own venue.

00:00:15.228 --> 00:00:19.430
Bring your phone for the passcode, and a laptop with Respondus lockdown installed.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.531
Do the practice test first.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.969
Transfer is the big skill.

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:27.038
A concept shown with Telstra might be asked about Qantas.

00:00:27.088 --> 00:00:29.893
Know the concept, not just the example.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.390
Aim for three to four hundred words an answer, and answer every part.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.863
Concepts are tested.

00:00:35.913 --> 00:00:38.044
Dates and career paths are not.

00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:40.268
Read the question carefully.

00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:42.969
Why did X do this wants the speaker's reasoning.

00:00:43.019 --> 00:00:45.826
Could Y do it too wants your own justified view.

00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:50.017
And model questions want the model applied accurately, tied to the outcome.

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:53.663
Revise every lecture, plus the workshop questions.

00:00:53.713 --> 00:00:54.889
Good luck.
